# --- Node ---
# No trailing slash: a worktree links node_modules to the primary checkout, and a symlink is a FILE.
# `node_modules/` matched directories only, so that link was committed as a 120000 blob holding an absolute
# path — a fresh clone would get a dangling symlink, and on the author's machine a silent shared dependency
# state across checkouts.
node_modules
.npm/
.node_repl_history
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

# --- Secrets / local config ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
*.cer

# --- Excavator runtime output ---
# Default workdir (`--workdir`, defaults to ./.work): run directories,
# prompts, checkpoints, caches and source excerpts. They contain local absolute
# paths and high-volume intermediate evidence and are never committed. The legacy
# `.excavator-work`/`excavator-work` names stay ignored for older workspaces.
.work/
.excavator-work/
excavator-work/
**/runs/
**/cache/


# Local request files (`request.example.json` is the tracked template).
/request.json
/request.*.json
!/request.example.json

# --- CodeGraph index ---
.codegraph/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# --- Test / tooling scratch ---
# ANCHORED to the repo root on purpose. This rule exists for the coverage reporter's own output, which lands
# here and nowhere else. Unanchored, it also hid every `*/coverage/` directory in the tree — and a run directory
# keeps its read-coverage residual under exactly that name, so checked-in fixture runs went missing from a fresh
# clone while staying green locally. That was patched once with a negation for `eval/tests/fixtures/*/coverage/`,
# and the trap sprang a second time on `tests/fixtures/topic-catalog-mini/coverage/`, which the negation did not
# reach. A per-location negation is a list someone has to remember to extend; an anchor is not. Run directories
# under `.work/` are ignored wholesale by their own rule, so nothing needs this pattern to be recursive.
/coverage/
.nyc_output/
tmp/
.tmp/
*.log
